    <node id="Early Modern Period">
      <data key="d0">Early Modern Period</data>
      <data key="d1">time_period</data>
      <data key="d2">The Early Modern Period denotes a historical phase marked by several significant events and transitions starting with the rise of the Ottoman Empire in the late 15th century through to the early 18th century. This period is often characterized by important changes such as the fall of Constantinople (1453), advancements in science, exploration activities, and religious movements like the Reformation. Spanning approximately from the 16th century to 1500 AD, it represents a critical juncture bridging the Middle Ages with the advent of modernity in Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-52590c98797ad329a47cbd07f6be3002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a9de0b248b887e51ee6760c5946a74a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d7bb40fa0aa36bf5b0bb66bf7975fe</data>
