    <node id="Early Civilizations">
      <data key="d0">Early Civilizations</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The early civilizations, such as Sumer, are described as the initial complex human societies marked by permanent settlements and specialized roles. These civilizations formed independently in various regions across the globe. The descriptions collectively emphasize the development of early complex societies characterized by settled living and the emergence of distinct social roles, focusing on their formation in different parts of the world, with specific mention to Sumer.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7e64e2403dd590a083e0fbec3e790668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a9e131275579f7dd159a5310055f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c1a3500d7732daf2db9f25db73376bf</data>
