    <node id="Persia">
      <data key="d0">Persia</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity Persia, during certain historical periods, had complex relationships with both the Byzantine Empire and conqueror Timur. Initially, Persia was integrated into the Byzantine Empire and engaged in interactions that shaped their political and social landscapes, although specific details of these engagements are not provided. Later, Persia faced significant changes as it was conquered by Timur during the 1380s and 1390s, marking a period of occupation and upheaval in its history. These events reflect the broader context of Central Asian expansionism and geopolitical dynamics of the era.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c13c9d68535c84e9a2084524eeed3c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c0fbb619a916ac387c46ee41fe1af47</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Aksum Kingdom">
      <data key="d0">Aksum Kingdom</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">The Aksum Kingdom was a significant entity that emerged during this period, playing a crucial role alongside, and sometimes challenging, Mediterranean cultures as explained more thoroughly in Chapter 10.3. Located in sub-Saharan Africa, it extended its influence across various regions, contributing to the expanding global reach of its cultural and economic impact.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c13c9d68535c84e9a2084524eeed3c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f82fcaeaf8ded7ccd594a70788c5c5e9</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210780</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Himyar Kingdom">
      <data key="d0">Himyar Kingdom</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">The Himyar Kingdom was an important civilization or empire during the given time period, similar to other significant powers such as Aksum. Ruling over fertile territories, this kingdom played a crucial role in trade and commerce within its era. The discussions surrounding the Himyar Kingdom highlight its importance in both geographical influence and economic activity during its peak.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e145b893a5d86970d1fbdb22f489be05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c13c9d68535c84e9a2084524eeed3c86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ce17d4abf19bd659433a6eaa668ad9c</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210781</data>
    </node>
