    <node id="Rise and Message of Islam">
      <data key="d0">Rise and Message of Islam</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Rise and Message of Islam refers to a significant event marking the emergence and spread of Islamic teachings and beliefs, which historically represents the origin and expansion of the Islamic faith during this period. This process encompasses both the initial establishment of Islamic doctrine and its subsequent dissemination across various regions, contributing to the rich historical narrative of the rise and growth of Islam.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3dc7e2b0bdcb5cf6ffad76150023fc3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7114383587a4baf0af7064a88a7b0f99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c13c9d68535c84e9a2084524eeed3c86</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Arab-Islamic Conquests">
      <data key="d0">Arab-Islamic Conquests</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Arab-Islamic Conquests describes the expansionist actions of Arab groups under the new religious and political framework provided by Islam.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c13c9d68535c84e9a2084524eeed3c86</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210777</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Caliphates">
      <data key="d0">Caliphates</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The Caliphates were states ruled by caliphs, rulers who claimed religious legitimacy through relation to Muhammad’s successors, a key development during this period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c13c9d68535c84e9a2084524eeed3c86</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210777</data>
    </node>
