    <node id="Renaissance">
      <data key="d0">Renaissance</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Renaissance was a significant period from the 1300s to the 1600s that marked an important cultural and intellectual revival across Europe, with its origins rooted particularly in Italy during the 14th century before spreading throughout the continent. This transformative era saw a renewed interest and rediscovery of classical Greek and Roman achievements in various fields such as art, sciences, literature, and philosophy. Influenced by contributions from Byzantine refugees, the Renaissance contributed to substantial economic and cultural changes not only across Italy but also other parts of Europe. It fostered significant advancements that profoundly impacted European society, making the Renaissance a pivotal movement in shaping the intellectual and artistic landscape of the region during this time period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-23659b0349306744ecfc24e78e40bee3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54c526f99d90b73a6903c122c8847aeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a9de0b248b887e51ee6760c5946a74a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3acbd758cf8087488127fa375dda8fa</data>
