    <node id="Ancient Egypt">
      <data key="d0">Ancient Egypt</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">Ancient Egypt was a civilization that emerged along the lower Nile River valley in northeastern Africa during the fourth millennium BCE, bordering both the Mediterranean Sea and the Red Sea. Spanning thousands of years, this influential ancient kingdom is renowned for its remarkable architectural achievements such as the pyramids, as well as its sophisticated hieroglyphic script and rich cultural history. The early development of Ancient Egypt involved significant geographical changes and the emergence of political and cultural institutions, marking one of the world's earliest and most profound civilizations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-038356ebaf9b5df91192c77bd51ac651&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef781679ddcfd1150ef200f135d92a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262ce3f10c5cb95e159b65dfc03d5961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e64e2403dd590a083e0fbec3e790668</data>
