    </node>
    <node id="Aztec Account">
      <data key="d0">Aztec Account</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">First-hand accounts or narratives from Aztecs regarding their experiences during the Spanish Conquest, crucial for understanding indigenous perspectives.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a90cbba1d3f0a8cc50e947b7f0000a37</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Franklin D. Roosevelt">
      <data key="d0">Franklin D. Roosevelt</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Franklin D. Roosevelt, the 32nd President of the United States, played a pivotal role in leading the nation through significant periods such as the Great Depression and World War II. Renowned for his exceptional governance skills and visionary leadership, Roosevelt delivered a crucial speech on December 8, 1941, declaring war against Japan to Congress. This "Day of Infamy" address marked a defining moment in American history, underscoring Roosevelt's profound impact on the country during critical times.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a90cbba1d3f0a8cc50e947b7f0000a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7fc147e6b53d5322148aad649d8fde</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210795</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pearl Harbor Attack">
      <data key="d0">Pearl Harbor Attack</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_event</data>
      <data key="d2">A surprise military strike conducted by the Imperial Japanese Navy Air Service on the United States naval base at Pearl Harbor, which prompted the United States to enter World War II.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a90cbba1d3f0a8cc50e947b7f0000a37</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="December 7, 1941">
      <data key="d0">December 7, 1941</data>
      <data key="d1">time_period</data>
      <data key="d2">The specific date of December 7, 1941, when Pearl Harbor was attacked by Japanese forces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f7fc147e6b53d5322148aad649d8fde</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210789</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pearl Harbor, Hawaii">
      <data key="d0">Pearl Harbor, Hawaii</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Pearl Harbor, located in Hawaii, is a significant historical site that is famously known for the Japanese attack on the U.S. naval base there. This incident triggered the direct cause leading to the United States' entry into World War II.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7be7011f70cfcce0eac890c78360b7f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f7fc147e6b53d5322148aad649d8fde</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210796</data>
    </node>
