    </node>
    <node id="stone tools">
      <data key="d0">stone tools</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Early humans, particularly Homo erectus, utilized simple stone tools for multiple tasks, with grinding plants being one of their primary uses. These stone tools hold significant value as artifacts in the archaeological study of early human cultures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-135eaddcc02a505fd05af47a63a3f85a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-990942779714eb1b55832fae0d8365e4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210803</data>
    </node>
    <node id="cooperative behavior">
      <data key="d0">cooperative behavior</data>
      <data key="d1">textbook_structure</data>
      <data key="d2">Cooperation among Homo erectus-such as hunting and foraging together-is a key organizing concept in understanding their social structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-135eaddcc02a505fd05af47a63a3f85a</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210798</data>
