      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Homo heidelbergensis, a possible ancestor of both Neanderthals and modern humans, lived between about 600,000 and 200,000 years ago in Europe, Africa, and Asia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7f9a47fe3a9c9c64cc2975619f1c44a3</data>
