    <node id="&lt;&quot;Hunter-gatherers&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Hunter-gatherers"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"cultural_or_religious_movement"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">Hunter-gatherers refer to pre-agricultural nomadic or semi-nomadic groups who survived by foraging for wild plants, hunting animals, and occasionally fishing. This lifestyle was practiced by early humans and characterized by their adaptability to varying climates and environments. These groups inhabited the Eastern Woodlands region during a specific time period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3686f653ac3553789cf9e605b69e032b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33e4049b688c17cc32c7d79fae4c8471</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210804</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;FIGURE_2_9_Tools&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;FIGURE_2_9_Tools&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;historical_concept_or_event&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">These tools are from the Mousterian period and date back between 250,000 to 50,000 years ago. They include stone scrapers used by early humans for cleaning and working leather.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d050ba72d7011fbfc01fd9092fd65a57</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
