    <node id="&lt;Controlled_Fires&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Controlled_Fires&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;historical_concept_or_event&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">"Controlled fires" were used by prehistoric humans at least 125,000 years ago based on archaeological evidence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d050ba72d7011fbfc01fd9092fd65a57</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210799</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;Fire_Usage_Benefits&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Fire_Usage_Benefits&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;historical_concept_or_event&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">Fire was used for warming in cold climates, scaring off predators, and cooking meat. It played a significant role in early human survival and development.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d050ba72d7011fbfc01fd9092fd65a57</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210799</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;Fire_Making_Tools&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Fire_Making_Tools&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;historical_concept_or_event&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">Fire-hardening wooden spears and treating stone for crafting tools were methods used by early humans to improve their technology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d050ba72d7011fbfc01fd9092fd65a57</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210799</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;Social_Gatherings_Fire&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Social_Gatherings_Fire&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;historical_concept_or_event&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">Fire facilitated bonding through social gatherings, promoting stronger social connections among early human communities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d050ba72d7011fbfc01fd9092fd65a57</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210799</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;Early_Human_Language&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Early_Human_Language&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;historical_concept_or_event&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">Complex languages used by modern humans began to develop around 100,000 years ago. No specific language is mentioned, but it refers to the development of linguistic capacities in early humans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d050ba72d7011fbfc01fd9092fd65a57</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210799</data>
