      <data key="d0">"Dolní Věstonice"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">"Dolní Věstonice is a site in Moravia, Czech Republic, where the Venus of Dolní Věstonice was discovered. This location offers context for the dating and cultural significance of the artifact."|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a7ed9ed426c677dfb751ca0d0f6c66e</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210800</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Danubian Neolithic Culture&quot;|&gt;">
      <data key="d0">"Danubian Neolithic Culture"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">"The Danubian Neolithic culture refers to a prehistoric culture in the area surrounding the Danube River, which thrived during the Neolithic period and is represented by various artifacts like the Venus of Dolní Věstonice."|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a7ed9ed426c677dfb751ca0d0f6c66e</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210800</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Central Russian Sites&quot;|&gt;">
      <data key="d0">"Central Russian Sites"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">"Central Russian sites where similar female figurines have been found provide additional insights into the widespread cultural practices associated with these early artifacts. These find locations support the theory that these artifacts held significant meaning for prehistoric societies, possibly related to fertility or other symbolic meanings."|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a7ed9ed426c677dfb751ca0d0f6c66e</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210800</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;Neolithic Period&quot;|&gt;">
      <data key="d0">"Neolithic Period"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">time_period"|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">"The Neolithic period, which spans from around 10,000 to 2,000 BCE in Europe, witnessed significant cultural shifts including the advent of agriculture and settled communities. Artifacts like the Venus figurines are key evidence in understanding this era."|&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8a7ed9ed426c677dfb751ca0d0f6c66e</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
