    <node id="Social Hierarchies">
      <data key="d0">Social Hierarchies</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Presence of new social hierarchies suggested by the artwork on the Art of Ur box.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1c1a3500d7732daf2db9f25db73376bf</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ur and nearby areas">
      <data key="d0">Ur and nearby areas</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">References to Ur and the region surrounding it indicate these places where social stratification was developing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5cc80f4856e6c9df805d419244928154</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Mexico">
      <data key="d0">Mexico</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">A specific geographical region where early complex societies such as the Olmec, Maya, and Aztec arose.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89a9e131275579f7dd159a5310055f45</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Olmec">
      <data key="d0">Olmec</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">One of the earliest known major civilizations in ancient Mexico, contributing to Mesoamerican culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-89a9e131275579f7dd159a5310055f45</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Inca">
      <data key="d0">Inca</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The Inca were one of the most prominent pre-Columbian civilizations in South America, distinguished by their unparalleled architectural achievements and extensive road systems. This civilization, renowned for its mastery in stonemasonry, reached its zenith when centered in Cuzco. Their impressive architectural feats and central city of Cuzco played crucial roles in establishing and maintaining their power throughout the region.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9262b57773b73a3ec93d925625b303fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a9e131275579f7dd159a5310055f45</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210815</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fertile Crescent">
      <data key="d0">Fertile Crescent</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">"The Fertile Crescent is a broad swath of land now in Iraq, Syria, Israel, Palestine, and Turkey where the world’s first cities were located including Çatalhöyük and Jericho."|</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b63f6d20ffb060f0c413763b316d411</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Göbekli Tepe">
      <data key="d0">Göbekli Tepe</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Göbekli Tepe is a monumental architecture site in southeast Turkey built by hunter-gatherer cultures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2b63f6d20ffb060f0c413763b316d411</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
