    <node id="Mesopotamia">
      <data key="d0">Mesopotamia</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Mesopotamia refers to an ancient region located between the Tigris and Euphrates rivers, encompassing parts of modern-day Iraq, eastern Syria, southeastern Turkey, and southwestern Iran. This historical region includes key locations such as where the Akkadian Empire was situated and is known for its pivotal role in the development of early civilizations. Mesopotamia influenced neighboring cultures through significant cultural and religious exchanges and trade routes that facilitated the movement of goods like tin and copper.

One of Mesopotamia's important contributions was influencing the Indus Valley civilization, likely through both cultural exchange and direct trade. The region also connected with the Eastern Mediterranean via vital trade routes, importing resources from areas including Canaan and exporting goods such as tin and copper. Through these interactions, Mesopotamian civilizational advancements notably impacted neighboring cultures and facilitated the spread of ideas, beliefs, and technological developments across a wide geographic area.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03e05c621c24bf3d1e73a7ca94fea65b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3a4ace18f781f226af8fab221b9ba4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-756f0b26d168efc2bc1d5ec8a2aa2219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce95f4fd988337875531ba7f4b862b38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f351e39bc01d0781d675dfb68a1bff58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fef781679ddcfd1150ef200f135d92a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-921eca26480da1b32897b0b58823f7d8</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210821</data>
    </node>
    <node id="common land">
      <data key="d0">common land</data>
      <data key="d1">concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Common land refers to communal areas where Hittite villagers collectively owned property, often worked together on agricultural activities. This practice indicates social organization and distribution of resources among the community members.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9872940bfb117b42b5b2cfcd147aa2ff</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
