    <node id="TheFindingofMoses Painting by Lawrence Alma-Tadema">
      <data key="d0">TheFindingofMoses Painting by Lawrence Alma-Tadema</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The 1904 painting 'The Finding of Moses' by Lawrence Alma-Tadema is an artistic representation of the biblical narrative, illustrating Moses being discovered by Pharaoh's daughter.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-101f85f166b49ff1dfbecddc6687ab0f</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210856</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Pharaohs Daughter's Action">
      <data key="d0">Pharaohs Daughter's Action</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The actions of Pharaoh's daughter in adopting and raising Moses are a significant historical concept or event, symbolizing themes of compassion and salvation within the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-101f85f166b49ff1dfbecddc6687ab0f</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210856</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Moses Birth and Early Life">
      <data key="d0">Moses Birth and Early Life</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The events surrounding the birth and early life of Moses, as described in Exodus 2:1-10, are key historical concepts related to significant moments in ancient Egyptian and Hebrew relations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-101f85f166b49ff1dfbecddc6687ab0f</data>
