    <node id="Peloponnesian War">
      <data key="d0">Peloponnesian War</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Peloponnesian War, fought from 431 to 404 BCE, was a significant conflict between the Athenian Empire and the Peloponnesian League led by Sparta. This prolonged warfare reshaped ancient Greek politics and society. Additionally, this period of history also witnessed notable advancements in art and literature, reflecting the complex interplay of cultural and political developments during this time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1b923a222fa396828cfac46f7a026c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3097b7631833d13406561b217f399efa</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210889</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Ancient Egyptian Art">
      <data key="d0">Ancient Egyptian Art</data>
      <data key="d1">cultural_or_religious_movement</data>
      <data key="d2">Ancient Egyptian Art is characterized by its strict conventions, such as arms held close to the body and a parallel stance for feet, influencing early Greek sculptural techniques.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d1b923a222fa396828cfac46f7a026c9</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210884</data>
    </node>
