      <data key="d1">time_period</data>
      <data key="d2">The Hellenistic period is a significant era that began following Alexander the Great's death, characterized by the widespread dissemination of Greek culture across the Mediterranean and Near East regions. This period also witnessed the consolidation of Greek cities under the governance of various Hellenistic kingdoms, alongside notable advancements in religious practices and beliefs.</data>
