    <node id="Hannibals Invasion of Rome">
      <data key="d0">Hannibals Invasion of Rome</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">"Hannibal's Invasion of Rome refers to the military campaign in which Hannibal led his army from Hispania over the Alps into Italy during the Second Punic War, leading to significant battles such as those at Trebia, Trasimene, and ultimately, Zama.")</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7595511c6280259b348ea8ca3413a6d3</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Second Punic War">
      <data key="d0">Second Punic War</data>
      <data key="d1">military_conflict</data>
      <data key="d2">A war between Carthage and Rome from 218 to 201 BC featuring the key figures of Hannibal and Scipio Africanus, resulting in significant battles and campaigns across Italy and North Africa.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7595511c6280259b348ea8ca3413a6d3</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Hannibal">
      <data key="d0">Hannibal</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Hannibal was a notable Carthaginian general during the Second Punic War against Rome, recognized for his tactical brilliance and strategic胆略。作为第二次布匿战争中的主要指挥官，他带领迦太基军队深入罗马领土，展现了卓越的军事才能和领导力。这些行动不仅体现了汉尼拔出色的军事策略，也使他在历史上留下了深刻的印记。</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7595511c6280259b348ea8ca3413a6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094b316ebd1084db7394e7e033e7e84b</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210892</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Scipio Africanus">
      <data key="d0">Scipio Africanus</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Publius Cornelius Scipio, commonly known as Scipio Africanus, was a key military leader during the later period of the Second Punic War. He is roughly contemporaneous with Hannibal Barca and played a pivotal role in Rome's ultimate victory over Carthage at the Battle of Zama, decisively ending the conflict in favor of Rome. His actions provided crucial context for broader conflict history between these two powers during the 3rd century BCE, though his activities are not directly related to events in that specific century. Scipio Africanus's victories, especially the decisive battle against Hannibal at Zama, solidified his legacy as one of Rome’s most prominent and influential generals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7595511c6280259b348ea8ca3413a6d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094b316ebd1084db7394e7e033e7e84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-102a3de218fabdb69815ca7d8d632b0a</data>
