    <node id="&lt;Rome&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Rome&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Rome is a geographical location originally situated within Italy but later expanding to encompass much of the Mediterranean world. Historically, it was the capital city of Italy for centuries and has been one of the largest cities in Europe. Rome holds significant importance not only due to its association with ancient empires such as the Roman Empire but also as the center of Christianity, represented by Vatican City. The city is renowned for its rich cultural heritage, including ancient traditions, historical sites like the Colosseum and Roman Forum, art, cuisine, and artistic achievements that contribute to its distinct identity.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-509aec8b178d8914185dac21879dedd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d6af87b20cd5c5556a01a3b05d06cc0</data>
