    <node id="&lt;textbook_structure&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;textbook_structure&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">textbook_structure</data>
      <data key="d2">The textbook structure discussed here focuses on two distinct historical themes: a comparative analysis of perspectives on Chinggis Khan and an examination of Octavian's (later known as Augustus) rule after 31 BCE. The first part of the description refers to "Comparative Analysis of Perspectives on Chinggis Khan," outlining an academic framework designed to explore various viewpoints surrounding this historical figure. This framework likely includes a comprehensive discussion of different scholarly interpretations, sources, and theories about Chinggis Khan's life and influence.

The second part describes the textbook structure centered around Octavian's rise to power following the decisive Battle of Actium in 31 BCE. This section details the significant appointments made by Octavian within the Senate, detailing the titles and powers he assumed as Augustus, thereby consolidating his control over Rome. The focus is on understanding how Octavian transformed himself from a military leader into a ruler with vast political and administrative authority.

Both descriptions indicate the presence of multiple academic sources or perspectives that are utilized to provide an in-depth analysis and understanding of these historical figures and their legacies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5914a1bc816edf3338d898be6d68146b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89576c0d4225b9ce6218c684fd4f58b7</data>
