    <node id="Thermopylae">
      <data key="d0">Thermopylae</data>
      <data key="d1">Spartan resistance</data>
      <data key="d2">The battle of Thermopylae involved the allied armies of Greece resisting the forces of Xerxes, a Persian king, particularly excluding Athens and Thebes. This significant military engagement highlighted Spartan military prowess and their tenacious resistance against foreign invaders, playing an integral role in shaping Spartan cultural identity. The conflict took place during the Greco-Persian Wars and is renowned for the valiant stand made by the Spartans under King Leonidas I against overwhelming odds.</data>
