    <node id="Titus">
      <data key="d0">Titus</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Titus was a Roman Emperor who reigned from 79 to 81 AD. He is notably remembered for dedicating the Colosseum in 80 CE with a long series of gladiatorial games lasting one hundred days to celebrate its official opening. Additionally, Titus gained prominence through his military campaigns against the Jews, culminating in the sacking of Jerusalem. His triumphs were commemorated by the Arch of Titus, which stands as a significant historical monument in Rome.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4f47473987e3a9f7e2d495ebfe8eb083&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7e64d0c2e104d943718b5901bc66b8c</data>
