    <node id="Constantine">
      <data key="d0">Constantine</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Constantine was an emperor of Rome who reigned from 306 to 337 AD and emerged during the internal conflicts among the tetrarchs in the Roman Empire. Known for his significant contributions to Christianity, Constantine played a crucial role in its spread within the empire, convening the First Council of Nicaea and contributing to the Christianization process. His reign included issuing the Edict of Milan, which marked an important step towards establishing Christianity as the state religion of Rome.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fa8b96093ad85d351d71a70ae72eb655&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76ce6c5d8fc29b6728dc6d89f3cbb2c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7e64d0c2e104d943718b5901bc66b8c</data>
