    <node id="Inca Empire">
      <data key="d0">Inca Empire</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The Inca Empire was an expansive administrative and geographical area created through conquest in South America, particularly ruling over a significant portion of western regions during the 15th to early 16th centuries, notably under the rule of Pachacuti Yupanqui. This empire faced numerous challenges in the 1530s, including internal conflicts and foreign conquest by Spanish forces led by Francisco Pizarro. The Inca Empire was characterized by its extensive political control over diverse territories and its military prowess, as evident from figures like those depicting Inca soldiers and administrative regions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a0eb56c52113d1fc2efc13b6051efae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81ff6d082654c526c4224665019c04f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9f934b57bac158210269fad101dae91</data>
