    <node id="&lt;cultural_or_religious_movement&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;cultural_or_religious_movement&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">cultural_or_religious_movement</data>
      <data key="d2">Cultural_or_religious_movement refers to a range of significant movements that have had profound impacts on society, politics, and spirituality across different times and geographical areas. For instance, Egyptian symbolism, associated with deities such as the god Re and the asp, significantly influenced political figures like Cleopatra, highlighting the intersection between religious beliefs and governance in ancient Egypt.

The Enlightenment was an intellectual movement that emerged in Europe during the 17th and 18th centuries. This cultural movement emphasized the power of reason, critical thinking, science, and skepticism towards traditional institutions and practices, aiming to challenge and reform established societal norms and beliefs.

Additionally, Hinduism is classified as one of the major world religions, primarily practiced in India. Known for its rich tapestry of philosophical and spiritual teachings that have evolved over thousands of years, it has significantly influenced social and cultural practices in the subcontinent.

Lastly, the Islamicization_of_indonesia illustrates the historical process through which Islam spread across Indonesia over several centuries, transforming the religious landscape and socio-political structures of the region. This movement demonstrates how religious beliefs can integrate into existing societies, resulting in substantial cultural and political changes.

In summary, these entities highlight diverse cultural and religious movements that have shaped various aspects of human history, from ancient symbolism to modern religious practices, across different geographical regions such as Egypt, Europe, India, and Indonesia.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b8ad3f8265df80ff0cbd95a7914a6123&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5914a1bc816edf3338d898be6d68146b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89576c0d4225b9ce6218c684fd4f58b7</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210909</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Nazca Lines">
      <data key="d0">Nazca Lines</data>
      <data key="d1">textbook_structure</data>
      <data key="d2">The Nazca Lines are a collection of large artistic representations, often featuring geometric patterns or depictions of animals such as birds, fish, and cats. These enigmatic designs were created by the Nazca people in the desert ground of modern southern Peru during the period from 200 BCE to 600 CE.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-61af3f4c1b1189c9bb78051c623bf7d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab2455895eb8921de59c456fa3781d0</data>
