    <node id="Sanhaja">
      <data key="d0">Sanhaja</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Sanhaja refers to one of two groupings of nomadic Berber tribes that founded certain West African kingdoms in conjunction with the Masmuda, and they also served as the primary nomadic group in the western Sahara responsible for handling trans-Saharan trade transport.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ad97ea1ef8e2c731dddc24e3eecbe4f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68be3898587a9f6e093512ef1a1060f3</data>
