    <node id="Gao">
      <data key="d0">Gao</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Gao is an entity located near the border of empires, notably being annexed by Mali and subsequently serving as the capital of the Songhai Empire. Known for its crucial role in the medieval trade network, Gao functioned as a pivotal trading site where camel caravans would stop to unload goods and replenish supplies before continuing their journeys. Historically, in 1438, Gao and Timbuktu were both abandoned by Mali due to strategic shifts or political changes within the empire.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0574b1f8c885767e594c6d93856176c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915948e7d5ef4ba882727621163189e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68be3898587a9f6e093512ef1a1060f3</data>
