    <node id="Vandals">
      <data key="d0">Vandals</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figures</data>
      <data key="d2">The Vandals, an entity originally hailing from central Europe, are noted for their significant presence during the early part of Justinian's reign. These Vandals controlled Carthage and extensive territories in North Africa before they were defeated by Byzantine forces. Their military campaign played a crucial role in Justinian's reconquest efforts. The Vandals moved through Gaul and Spain and eventually established their kingdom in North Africa following their crossing of the Rhine in 406 AD.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8b93582db5d7a873cf44814a77997d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622311a2741b1845b3a8c00c6e5d7b93</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210954</data>
    </node>
