    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Parthians&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Parthians"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"civilization_or_empire"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"The Parthians were a Persian dynasty that controlled the Parthian Empire from the 3rd century BC to the 3rd century AD. Their rise came after conficts with the Seleucids and their decentralized governance through satraps."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Seleucids&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Seleucids"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"civilization_or_empire"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"'The Seleucids were the Hellenistic dynasty that controlled a large empire in Asia after Alexander the Great's death. Their conflict with the Parthians led to the decline of the Seleucid Empire and the rise of the Parthian Empire."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Sasanians&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Sasanians"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"civilization_or_empire"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"'The Sasanians are known for founding the Sassanid Empire, reigning from 224 CE to 651 CE. The empire was characterized by a centralized state structure and extensive trade networks."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Ardashir I&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Ardashir I"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"historical_figure"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"'Ardashir I is considered the founder of the Sassanid Empire. His conquests expanded Sasanian territory, leading to conflicts with the Roman Empire and notable successes such as capturing Valerian."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Shapur I&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Shapur I"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"historical_figure"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"'Shapur I was a Sasanian emperor who succeeded his father Ardashir I. Under his rule, notable events included the capture of Emperor Valerian of Rome in 260 CE, marking significant Roman-Sasanian conflict."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Silk Roads&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Silk Roads"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"historical_concept_or_event"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"'The Silk Roads were a network of trade routes connecting East and West. They facilitated extensive cultural and commercial exchanges between the Sasanians, Romans, Chinese, and other civilizations."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Constantinople&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Constantinople"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"geographical_location"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"'Constantinople was the capital city of the Eastern Roman Empire. As an influential center in 6th-century Byzantine society, it held great significance for both the empress Theodora and emperor Justinian I."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Nomadic tribes&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Nomadic tribes"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"historical_concept_or_event"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"'The nomadic tribes of the Iranian plateau coexisted with Sasanian rulers. They represented a significant demographic presence in regions bordering urban centers under their control."</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f3483082d977617409e75f5948382d4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210950</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;entity_name&gt;Roman Empire">
      <data key="d0">&lt;entity_name&gt;Roman Empire</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;entity_type&gt;historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;entity_description&gt;The Roman Empire at its maximum territorial extent, encompassing Europe, North Africa, and Western Asia. It is known for its significant political, military, cultural, and technological advancements during the peak period of 200 AD.&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-35dabc1121dedf5713913da08d2b42e7</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
