    </node>
    <node id="Zoroastrianism">
      <data key="d0">Zoroastrianism</data>
      <data key="d1">cultural_or_religious_movement</data>
      <data key="d2">Zoroastrianism is a pre-Islamic Iranian religion that played a significant and unique role as one of the major religious traditions during Late Antiquity. Named after its founder Zarathustra, who is known as Zoroaster in Greek, Zoroastrianism originated among the ancient Persians. This comprehensive description integrates the core information from all provided descriptions while maintaining coherence and accuracy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-64b6a2af1c3cece75a3cbd9b707b8713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4adb7fe027038f7279ff275f67a969f</data>
