    <node id="&lt;&quot;Arab-Muslim conquests&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Arab-Muslim conquests"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"historical_concept_or_event"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"The term Arab-Muslim conquests refers to a series of military campaigns led by the Islamic caliphate and its allies from the 7th century CE, which resulted in the establishment of Muslim rule over large parts of the former Roman and Sasanian empires. The events are marked by a blend of military might, political cunning, and strategic alliances that led to significant transformations in the geopolitical landscape of the time."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-927613aa4aec81a8719529ae83d4bfd6</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Iraq&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Iraq"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"geographical_location"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"Iraq is a country in Western Asia. It was central to the initial spread of Islam following the Arab-Muslim conquests, becoming an integral part of the rapidly expanding Islamic state."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-927613aa4aec81a8719529ae83d4bfd6</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Persia (Sasanian Empire)&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Persia (Sasanian Empire)"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"civilization_or_empire"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"The Sasanian Empire, known as Persia in Western sources, was a major political power in Western Asia from 224 to 651 CE. It was one of the last great Persian empires before the region was eventually conquered by the forces of Islam."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-927613aa4aec81a8719529ae83d4bfd6</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Byzantine Empire (Byzantine Eastern Territories)&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Byzantine Empire (Byzantine Eastern Territories)"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"civilization_or_empire"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"The Byzantine Empire, also known as the Eastern Roman Empire, was a continuation of the Roman Empire in the East. It controlled much of what is now eastern Europe and parts of Western Asia and North Africa."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-927613aa4aec81a8719529ae83d4bfd6</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;&quot;Islamic state&quot;&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;"Islamic state"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;"historical_concept_or_event"&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;"The Islamic state denotes the political order established by Muslims and characterized by the rule of Sharia law, with an emphasis on governance according to Islamic principles. The concept developed during the Arab-Muslim conquests as Muslim rulers sought to shape their dominions through religious and legal frameworks."&gt;</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-927613aa4aec81a8719529ae83d4bfd6</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
