    <node id="&lt;Baghdad&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Baghdad&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Baghdad was a crucial city that served as the capital of the Abbasid Caliphate until 836 AD. Founded as both an administrative center and a cultural hub during the Abbasid era, Baghdad became a significant focal point for trade, culture, and learning. It is renowned for its remarkable scholarly achievements across various fields during this period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4809fc11398ec2c07172fc5d5bf5447f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a51f56123d8110f2ea915388f363a913</data>
