    <node id="Delhi Sultanate">
      <data key="d0">Delhi Sultanate</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The Delhi Sultanate was a powerful Muslim empire established in northern India during the Middle Ages, spanning from Punjab to Bengal and existing from 1206 to 1526. This historical empire is recognized for its growth and responses over this period. Notably, it faced targeted but unsuccessful attempts at conquest by several Mongol Khanates, including significant military actions led by Timur against Delhi. Despite these challenges, the Delhi Sultanate maintained political stability and experienced substantial urban development. Spanning much of the Indian subcontinent under Muslim governance, the rule of the Delhi Sultanate was characterized by expansion, political consolidation, and notable advancements in urban areas.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42369c47f2f60a9ab4ac526953bf6b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6804ed94e025d37cfcb352ad735e3ba4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3940f5bfcfa4bc96e49773142fb8d2a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbaccac96c9ea8e056f368393c0b33b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c0fbb619a916ac387c46ee41fe1af47</data>
