    <node id="Queen Ezana">
      <data key="d0">Queen Ezana</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Queen Ezana ruled the Aksumite Empire, expanding trade and leaving behind her Christian mark through inscriptions and monuments. Her reign exemplified Axumite power in the 4th century AD.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68886ae6bf0868f51bdd288cf9f2091f</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Srivijaya Kingdom">
      <data key="d0">Srivijaya Kingdom</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The Srivijaya Kingdom was a maritime empire that dominated Southeast Asia from the 7th to the 13th centuries. Flourishing through its control over trade routes, particularly across the Strait of Malacca and Java Sea, it played a key role in regional history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68886ae6bf0868f51bdd288cf9f2091f</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210981</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Palk Strait">
      <data key="d0">Palk Strait</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Palk Strait is an oceanic strait that separates India from Sri Lanka. In the context of Srivijaya's trade monopoly, navigable through with ships from Java, this body of water was crucial for facilitating maritime commerce.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-68886ae6bf0868f51bdd288cf9f2091f</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210981</data>
