    <node id="Outremer">
      <data key="d0">Outremer</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Outremer is a historical designation representing the various Crusader States established in the Levant and other territories following the conquests during the First and Second Crusades. These territories were initially targeted by expulsions and massacres, as documented in historical records. The term Outremer encompasses multiple states and regions occupied by the First Crusade and its descendants, signifying a significant geographical shift and new focus for European nobles and knights drawn to these 'overseas' or non-European domains. This collective entity highlights the political and social transformations brought about by the Crusades, marking a pivotal period in medieval history where European powers sought to establish dominion in lands outside Europe.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-aeb38d9c22dbab062c46fb4a7bdfb465&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5b2b430185118342f9094519e5e975&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70f9dac922d55e716828dd14b5668a0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b150c3e9d15dec1eaca94b8168bda0ba</data>
