    <node id="&lt;Mongol Empire&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Mongol Empire&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;civilization_or_empire&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">The Mongol Empire was a vast Eurasian empire that significantly expanded during two key periods: under Chinggis Khan from 1207 to 1227, and later under Kublai Khan who extended the empire's influence further across Central Asia and Eastern regions. Initially led by Chinggis Khan, the Mongol Empire conquered northern China and other areas beyond its initial borders during this era.

Under Kublai Khan, the Mongol Empire reached its zenith, encompassing extensive territories in Central Asia and East with diverse peoples and cultures under its rule. During his reign from 1260 to 1294, administrative practices that respected various racial backgrounds were implemented to manage such a vast domain, which included China. This comprehensive governance aimed at maintaining stability and effective control over the empire's extensive territories.

Both Chinggis Khan and Kublai Khan played pivotal roles in shaping the Mongol Empire into one of history's most expansive and influential powers, known for its military prowess and administrative innovations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c065aace43270eef7d2c60439e6d228b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475ef7f0df0edf6dfe1fe0174a98af67</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211001</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;Kara-Khitan Kingdom&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Kara-Khitan Kingdom&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;civilization_or_empire&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;The Kara-Khitan Kingdom, an empire conquered by the Mongols, where spoils were gathered upon absorption into the Mongol Empire.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c065aace43270eef7d2c60439e6d228b</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210993</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;Khwarazmia (Khwarezm)&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Khwarazmia (Khwarezm)&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;civilization_or_empire&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;Khwarazmia, a region targeted for conquest by the Mongols in 1219-1221, leading to hostilities due to the killing of envoys.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c065aace43270eef7d2c60439e6d228b</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210993</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&lt;Zhongdu&gt;">
      <data key="d0">&lt;Zhongdu&gt;</data>
      <data key="d1">&lt;geographical_location&gt;</data>
      <data key="d2">&lt;Zhongdu, a significant area conquered by the Mongol Empire where spoils were gathered. Zhongdu is important for its role in supplying imperial resources and wealth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c065aace43270eef7d2c60439e6d228b</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
