    <node id="Jaffa truce">
      <data key="d0">Jaffa truce</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">A ten-year truce between Muslims and Christians was established, prohibiting the rebuilding of Jerusalem’s city walls and leaving the city defenseless if attacked by Muslims.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fcb1c0aa30537ed564041e3f6b9c2246</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Cultural or religious exchange">
      <data key="d0">Cultural or religious exchange</data>
      <data key="d1">cultural_or_religious_movement</data>
      <data key="d2">The treaty allowed for Muslim practices such as Islamic worship and control over holy sites like Al-Aqsa Mosque and Dome of the Rock, symbolizing a period of cultural and religious exchange between Christian and Muslim communities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-fcb1c0aa30537ed564041e3f6b9c2246</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783210999</data>
    </node>
