    <node id="Mansa Musa">
      <data key="d0">Mansa Musa</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Mansa Musa is a historical figure renowned for his extensive wealth and powerful influence during the medieval period in West Africa. This prominent ruler undertook a notable pilgrimage around 1324-1325, characterized by his charitable giveaways and diplomatic missions. His generous donations of vast amounts of gold significantly reduced the prices in Cairo for several years following his journey, showcasing both his wealth and his far-reaching impact on trade and economy.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-653e423a3526fec9af080bbf288c37ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4740aa455c5d7e5c0aa1852e0ca7c696</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
