    </node>
    <node id="Soninke Ghanaians">
      <data key="d0">Soninke Ghanaians</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">The Soninke Ghanaians converted to Islam due to the religious and military actions of the Almoravids, marking a turning point for this group within Ghana's political structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d32d7ef2fac445505a9bd6f9b878a6f4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211004</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sosso Kingdom">
      <data key="d0">Sosso Kingdom</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Sosso Kingdom was a short-lived state established by Soumaoro, who belonged to the southern Soninke branch. This kingdom came into existence following the waning power of the Ghana Empire, expanding into areas previously controlled by Ghana. The Sosso Kingdom played a significant role in laying the groundwork for the rise of the Mali Empire by exerting influence over former Ghana territories during its brief tenure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-42e94d3dccf53e38234edf815e468339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d32d7ef2fac445505a9bd6f9b878a6f4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211008</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Eighth Century">
      <data key="d0">Eighth Century</data>
      <data key="d1">time_period</data>
      <data key="d2">The eighth century started the rise of Ghana as a leading power in western Africa, laying the foundation for its later expansion and influence.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d32d7ef2fac445505a9bd6f9b878a6f4</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211004</data>
    </node>
