    <node id="Fourteenth Century">
      <data key="d0">Fourteenth Century</data>
      <data key="d1">time_period</data>
      <data key="d2">The Fourteenth Century, spanning from 1300 to 1399, is noted for its significance in both European and Chinese history. This period is characterized by a rapid succession of crises, which include major climatic changes and pandemics affecting various regions. Additionally, the Fourteenth Century marks a pivotal transition in European history, while also being associated with the beginning of the Ming dynasty in China, as Zhu Yuanzhang became its first emperor during this time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb1aed2461d605387294e530dbb57f99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c35939e482e2a77512480fac9dae902&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f4d8efbf198b190c61398bff7ef3200</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211017</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Climate Change, Little Ice Age">
      <data key="d0">Climate Change, Little Ice Age</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Climate Change, represented as the Little Ice Age, refers to environmental changes that took place during this time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0f4d8efbf198b190c61398bff7ef3200</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211011</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bubonic Plague">
      <data key="d0">Bubonic Plague</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Bubonic Plague is a significant historical event that occurred during the late 1340s, representing one of several crises faced in the Fourteenth Century. This catastrophic disease had profound impacts on both the Mamluk Empire and Europe, striking at pivotal moments in history and reshaping societies across these regions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c136dfeff6dede53a0a73af631e7957d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f4d8efbf198b190c61398bff7ef3200</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211016</data>
    </node>
