    </node>
    <node id="1315">
      <data key="d0">1315</data>
      <data key="d1">time_period</data>
      <data key="d2">The year 1315, during which the Great Famine had a significant impact on England.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711e8b5f07c221ff8749b18f9665fc50</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211014</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Great Famine">
      <data key="d0">Great Famine</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Great Famine, which occurred between 1315 and 1317, was a severe food shortage that predominantly affected northern regions of Europe. This period of widespread famine significantly impacted daily life and economic conditions across these territories. The food scarcity resulted from crop failures attributed to the worsening environmental conditions during the Little Ice Age, characterized by colder temperatures and heavy rainfall. These adverse weather patterns severely hindered agricultural productivity, leading to a significant humanitarian crisis during this time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-711e8b5f07c221ff8749b18f9665fc50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f485cc659c371a55149fcc8ff3f200a5</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211020</data>
    </node>
