    <node id="Ming Dynasty">
      <data key="d0">Ming Dynasty</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">The Ming Dynasty was a period of rule in China spanning from the mid-14th to early 17th centuries. It is known for its significant cultural and technological achievements. This dynasty was established by Zhu Yuanzhang during the fourteenth century and ruled China as its primary empire throughout its duration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-cb1aed2461d605387294e530dbb57f99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d7bb40fa0aa36bf5b0bb66bf7975fe</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211023</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Suleymaniye Mosque">
      <data key="d0">Suleymaniye Mosque</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Suleymaniye Mosque is an architectural artifact built during the reign of Suleiman I, known for its Islamic elements like minarets and a large central dome, reflecting the influence of earlier religious structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72d7bb40fa0aa36bf5b0bb66bf7975fe</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211020</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Sumerian oracular tradition">
      <data key="d0">Sumerian oracular tradition</data>
      <data key="d1">cultural_or_religious_movement</data>
      <data key="d2">The reference to Solomon's temple as an influence on Hagia Sophia reflects the Sumerian oracular traditions in shaping religious architecture through time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-72d7bb40fa0aa36bf5b0bb66bf7975fe</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211021</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Gunpowder">
      <data key="d0">Gunpowder</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Gunpowder, an essential technological advance, was introduced in Europe primarily through texts brought back by Crusaders or via Muslim kingdoms established in Spain until the fifteenth century. This substance significantly influenced warfare and military strategy during the transition period from medieval to early modern times.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9659ee5a3cec87c5f65828322cee3bbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72d7bb40fa0aa36bf5b0bb66bf7975fe</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211025</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Incursions of the Seljuk Empire against the Byzantines">
      <data key="d0">Incursions of the Seljuk Empire against the Byzantines</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The incursions of the Seljuk Empire against the Byzantines refer to military actions by the Seljuk Empire against the Byzantine Empire, primarily taking place during the eleventh century within the larger narrative of shifting power dynamics. These territorial disputes and military campaigns are detailed in various sources, including descriptions found at URLs such as [http://example.com/1077_seljuk_invasion]. It is important to note that while some descriptions incorrectly attribute these incursions to the Fourteenth Century, historical records consistently place them in the eleventh century.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9ce8afb7df7219a173442d3c4ef86a29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b48f1c75c48a630bdea282765ade371c</data>
