    <node id="Battle of Ankara">
      <data key="d0">Battle of Ankara</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Battle of Ankara, which occurred in 1402, was a crucial military confrontation during which Timur's forces decisively defeated Bayezid I, who was the Ottoman Sultan at the time. This significant engagement took place in Anatolia and served as a pivotal turning point not only in the conflict between Timur and the Ottoman Empire but also in the broader narrative of the Ottoman Empire’s history. The capture of Bayezid I by Timur marked a crucial shift that had far-reaching consequences for both parties involved, heralding a period of instability within the Ottoman leadership and a significant setback for the empire's territorial and political ambitions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3781905eca1839631b0bed57e233e84b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-325c2f087ce183f26e739c5d7d7a119e</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211032</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Bayezid I">
      <data key="d0">Bayezid I</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">Bayezid I, also known as Bayezid I the Thunderbolt, was the Sultan of the Ottoman Empire from 1402 to 1404 and again after 1413. As a powerful conqueror in Anatolia, he clashed with Timur's forces at the Battle of Ankara, leading to his defeat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-325c2f087ce183f26e739c5d7d7a119e</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211024</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Black Sheep Turks">
      <data key="d0">Black Sheep Turks</data>
      <data key="d1">cultural_or_religious_movement</data>
      <data key="d2">The Black Sheep Turks, a Turcoman group, competed with the White Sheep Turks for control of Iran and were considered enemies by Timur.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-325c2f087ce183f26e739c5d7d7a119e</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
