    <node id="Madrasas">
      <data key="d0">Madrasas</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity, Madrasas, refers to educational institutions established in various locations. Notably, they were erected in Istanbul by a particular historical figure where Muslim scholars imparted knowledge in fields such as science, Islamic law, and theology. Additionally, the term is also associated with Timur's capital city of Samarkand, specifically flanking the central square known as Registan. This dual context highlights the diverse geographical distribution and educational focus of these institutions across different regions and periods.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e02f2af9c7712235155281a18fd34d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b67f0f7afc2d163b11e5f62d24179b37</data>
