    <node id="Black Death">
      <data key="d0">Black Death</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">The Black Death was a catastrophic pandemic that occurred in the mid-14th century, having profound impacts on the population, society, economy, and spiritual life of Europe and other regions including Asia, the Middle East, and North Africa. It is estimated to have reduced the European population by 30%-60%, leading to massive societal disruption and economic changes. At the time, many believed the epidemic was due to religious, astrological, or supernatural factors, reflecting a spiritual and social response that influenced communities across Europe during this critical historical period. Known for its wide-reaching effects on demographic and structural aspects of society, the Black Death left a lasting legacy in medieval history.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-3b7689ee0f0cb1dc256b2f6f742b501e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f485cc659c371a55149fcc8ff3f200a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b56f9a21e36a70c8e0f617fe96644340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d85eeeedc638b2dc40a70eec24196c37</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211021</data>
    </node>
