    </node>
    <node id="Timurid authority">
      <data key="d0">Timurid authority</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Following the collapse of Timurid authority, Ottoman state could now assert its control more broadly across both East and West.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8adac32853d2cbcb9cfc409ace493450</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211027</data>
    </node>
    <node id="kanun">
      <data key="d0">kanun</data>
      <data key="d1">textbook_structure</data>
      <data key="d2">Kanun, laws issued by Sultan Mehmed II, is a system he used to exert centralized authority over his domains, distinct from sharia law.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-8adac32853d2cbcb9cfc409ace493450</data>
