    <node id="Middle Eastern history">
      <data key="d0">Middle Eastern history</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_concept_or_event</data>
      <data key="d2">Middle Eastern history refers to the historical framework and events that provide a broader timeframe within which maps of the region are analyzed. This historical period encompasses significant changes and key events covering countries such as Iran, Iraq, Syria, Lebanon, Jordan, Israel, Palestine, Saudi Arabia, Egypt, and others from ancient times through modern periods. The focus is on illustrating major developments and turning points that have shaped the region's collective past.</data>
