    <node id="Tudors">
      <data key="d0">Tudors</data>
      <data key="d1">historical_figure</data>
      <data key="d2">The Tudors is a significant period in British history characterized by influential monarchs such as Henry VIII and Elizabeth I. Discussions often center around their reigns, policies, and their impact on England during this time.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Athens, Ancient Greece">
      <data key="d0">Athens, Ancient Greece</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Ancient Athens was one of the most influential city-states in Greece during classical times. Discussions often cover its democratic governance, philosophy, architecture, and contribution to Western culture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="China, Ancient China">
      <data key="d0">China, Ancient China</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Ancient China encompasses the early civilizations in China that left behind significant historical artifacts and cultural practices. It is a crucial location for discussions on the early development of Chinese society, technology, philosophy, and governance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Japan, Ancient Japan">
      <data key="d0">Japan, Ancient Japan</data>
      <data key="d1">geographical_location</data>
      <data key="d2">Ancient Japan refers to the period before the rise of modern nation-states and includes various early dynasties and cultures that significantly impact Japanese history. Discussions often cover its early religious practices, political structures, and cultural developments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Fifteen Minute History">
      <data key="d0">Fifteen Minute History</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">'Fifteen Minute History' provides audio content on a wide range of historical topics and periods. It offers insights into various civilizations, significant events, figures, and historical concepts in an engaging format.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Not Just the Tudors">
      <data key="d0">Not Just the Tudors</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">'Not Just the Tudors' is a podcast focusing on British history outside the Tudor period, providing detailed discussions on other monarchs, events, and historical figures relevant to English history beyond the famous Tudors.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The China History Podcast">
      <data key="d0">The China History Podcast</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">'The China History Podcast' covers various aspects of Chinese history from ancient times to modern periods. It delves into political development, social changes, cultural achievements, and significant historical events in China.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="The History of Rome">
      <data key="d0">The History of Rome</data>
      <data key="d1">source_or_artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">'The History of Rome' focuses on the historical journey of one of the greatest empires in history, offering comprehensive insights into its rise, fall, and lasting impact on Western civilization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Archaic Greece">
      <data key="d0">Archaic Greece</data>
      <data key="d1">civilization_or_empire</data>
      <data key="d2">The period in ancient Greek history that lasted from the end of the Dark Age (around 800 BCE) to the Persian invasion of Greece, marked by the establishment of city-states and significant cultural developments like the Olympics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c1d02d55a0d3b389107528715e89a23a</data>
      <data key="d4">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d5">1783211037</data>
