      <data key="d2">&lt;During the reign of Pope Gregory XI, there was an overlap in political and religious leadership between the Papacy and the Holy Roman Empire. The Emperor's role could indirectly influence church matters, though the direct interaction here is limited due to the specific nature of their positions.</data>
