    </edge>
    <edge source="Byzantine Empire" target="Seljuk Empire">
      <data key="d6">16.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Seljuk Empire and the Byzantine Empire engaged in significant competitive interactions for influence over Anatolia and the surrounding regions. These two empires both competed strategically and contested territories, with the Seljuk Empire extending its reach into Anatolia at the expense of the Byzantine Empire. These complex dynamics led to multifaceted cultural exchanges and conflicts between the two powers.</data>
      <data key="d8">competition,expansion,influence,interaction,territorial</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef569534db6161860971327c3bc8b184</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211089</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Byzantine Empire" target="Sultans">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Sultans often interacted with Byzantine officials on matters related to trade and diplomacy.</data>
      <data key="d8">diplomacy,interaction,trade</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef569534db6161860971327c3bc8b184</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211089</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Byzantine Empire" target="Caravansaries">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The caravansaries facilitated economic activities and diplomatic relations benefiting both Seljuk and Byzantine Empires.</data>
      <data key="d8">diplomacy,facilitate,relations</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-ef569534db6161860971327c3bc8b184</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211089</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Byzantine Empire" target="Macedonian Dynasty">
      <data key="d6">18.0</data>
      <data key="d7">During the Macedonian Dynasty, the Byzantine Empire underwent significant transformations characterized by the activities of key leaders such as Basil II and his successors. The Macedonian rulers directly governed the empire, significantly impacting its territorial integrity, political structure, military strength, and cultural advancements. Their reign witnessed both positive developments and challenges for the empire's stability and global influence. The leadership under the Macedonian Dynasty left a lasting impact on the Byzantine Empire, marking an era of notable achievement and complex dynamics within the realm.</data>
      <data key="d8">"Governance"|,"Leadership Impact"|</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99442760cad93ba2b6238a5063d5e7a3</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211093</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Byzantine Empire" target="Dynatoi">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Dynatoi were high-ranking officials in the Byzantine Empire who faced constraints during the Macedonian period but were later supported by less competent leaders, leading to social and military implications for the empire.</data>
      <data key="d8">"Political Alliances"|</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-99442760cad93ba2b6238a5063d5e7a3</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211093</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Byzantine Empire" target="Bayezid I, &quot;Thunderbolt&quot;">
      <data key="d6">14.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Bayezid I's military campaigns were targeting Constantinople and the Byzantine territories.</data>
      <data key="d8">campaigns,conquest</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-51a6e6c0f619a3b37e3ee2a7e7f19b5a</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211099</data>
    </edge>
