    </edge>
    <edge source="Neolithic Era" target="Cultural Or Religious Movement'&lt; Work">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">During the Neolithic era, societies developed complex cultural practices such as building religious monuments or observatories like the Tower of Jericho, as well as creating symbolic artifacts like decorated skulls.</data>
      <data key="d8">era-culture-religion</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-00b045edff27a3849cb01d2c87c94a5f</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211044</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Neolithic Era" target="Ancient Artisans'&lt; Work">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Artisans from the Neolithic period, including those who made artifacts like the decorated skull, played a crucial role in the development of cultural and religious practices during this era.</data>
      <data key="d8">craftsmanship-era</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-00b045edff27a3849cb01d2c87c94a5f</data>
