      <data key="d11">1783211047</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;lugals&gt;" target="First Dynasty of Ur">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The lugalshad, or rulers during the First Dynasty of Ur, had significant influence over resources and construction projects, reflecting the power dynamics within Sumerian society at that time.</data>
      <data key="d8">power-structure-resources</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a8ea083f226618d1b7e5a85496f09e4d</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211047</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Pu-Abi&gt;" target="First Dynasty of Ur">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Pu-Abi's tomb during the First Dynasty of Ur illustrates the wealth and status of some individuals during this period, indicating the social stratification within Sumerian society.</data>
      <data key="d8">social-stratification-tomb</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-a8ea083f226618d1b7e5a85496f09e4d</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
