    <edge source="Syria" target="Mesopotamia">
      <data key="d6">24.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Mesopotamia expanded its control over Syria during the First Empire Era through military or political means. This expansion facilitated the integration of Syrian territories into the Mesopotamian sphere of influence, enhancing the region's trade capabilities significantly. The interconnected trade routes between Mesopotamia and Syria ensured the efficient exchange of essential resources such as copper and tin, which were crucial for both regions' economic development and prosperity.</data>
      <data key="d8">Trade Network,expansion-geography</data>
