    </edge>
    <edge source="Assyrian Empire" target="Ashurbanipal">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Ashurbanipal was a key ruler of the Assyrian Empire, renowned for his military conquests and cultural legacy during the empire's zenith in the 7th century BCE. He ruled as part of what is often considered the Neo-Assyrian Period.</data>
      <data key="d8">royalty-period-legacy</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-23d1e6b89ed34f781b195088854edaee</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211051</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Assyrian Empire" target="Assyrian Arabian Battle">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The stone relief, depicting battles against nomadic Arabians, is a testament to the Assyrian Empire's military prowess during the Iron Age. It shows how the empire maintained control over vast territories through organized warfare.</data>
      <data key="d8">military-prowess-victory</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-23d1e6b89ed34f781b195088854edaee</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211051</data>
    </edge>
