    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Bronze 'Dancing Girl' artifact&gt;" target="&lt;Indus Valley Civilization&gt;">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Bronze 'Dancing Girl' artifact is a representation of the Indus Valley society during its period of complexity and fluid class structures. This artifact provides insight into the sophisticated social dynamics and hierarchical shifts characteristic of the Indus Valley Civilization. Both entities are intimately connected, with the Dancing Girl artifact serving as an important archaeological evidence that illustrates the societal complexities and evolving class systems within this ancient civilization.</data>
      <data key="d8">class structure,complex society,complexity</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6cbd9d663b9bcdcbd4f8a3f2604aa0a3</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211059</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Bronze 'Dancing Girl' artifact&gt;" target="&lt;Dancing Girl&gt;">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Refers to the same bronze figurine; the entity name specifies the depicted figure. The artifact represents this dancing girl</data>
      <data key="d8">dance</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6cbd9d663b9bcdcbd4f8a3f2604aa0a3</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211059</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;BhagavadGita&gt;" target="&lt;Vedas&gt;">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Bhagavad Gita draws upon Vedic traditions and scriptures to guide moral living.||&gt;&lt;religious_texts&gt;</data>
