    <edge source="Constantine" target="Council_of_Nicaea">
      <data key="d6">28.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Constantine, a key historical figure, convened the First Council of Nicaea. This council was instrumental in addressing theological disputes among bishops, particularly those related to Arianism, as well as solidifying religious orthodoxy through the establishment of doctrines such as those outlined in the Nicene Creed. The convening of this council by Constantine played a crucial role in shaping early Christian doctrine and consolidating the Church's position on central theological issues during that era.</data>
      <data key="d8">council_convocation,council_convocation_orthodoxy,legal_action,legal_theology,religious_control,religious_laws</data>
