    <edge source="1200 BCE" target="&quot;Olmec colossal head'">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Olmec colossal heads, created around 1200 BCE, are significant source or artifacts that represent a cultural or religious movement among the Olmec civilization. These monumental stone carvings serve as tangible evidence of the artistic and spiritual practices of this ancient Mesoamerican culture, embodying both their creative achievements and perhaps their deeply held beliefs or rituals.</data>
      <data key="d8">The Olmec colossal head is a significant artifact associated with this time period,The Olmec colossal head is a significant artifact associated with this time.,signifying aspects of Olmec culture and religion.</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-198d012fb68570600c9806ad61424ece</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211068</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="300 BCE" target="&quot;Maya stucco glyphs '">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Maya stucco glyphs from around 300 BCE are historical artifacts that provide insight into the ancient Mayan civilization. These glyphs, carved in limestone stucco, serve as sources of historical information and cultural heritage. Found or created during a period of early Classic Maya history, they offer valuable archaeological data about the societal, political, and religious aspects of the time.</data>
      <data key="d8">Maya stucco glyphs are cultural artifacts from the Maya civilization.,Maya stucco glyphs are part of the rich cultural and religious expressions of the Maya civilization.</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-198d012fb68570600c9806ad61424ece</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211068</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="1450 CE" target="&quot;Machu Picchu'">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Machu Picchu, constructed around 1450 CE, was a significant Incan site that played an important historical role. While the exact historical figures associated with its construction and usage are not definitively known, various sources and artifacts provide insights into the site's history and cultural significance. These descriptions from different sources collectively offer a comprehensive view of Machu Picchu during the 15th century CE.</data>
      <data key="d8">Machu Picchu is a significant architectural and archaeological site associated with this time period.,The construction of Machu Picchu reflects the advanced architectural,and urban planning skills of the Inca civilization during this time period.,engineering</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-198d012fb68570600c9806ad61424ece</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211069</data>
    </edge>
