    <edge source="&lt;Congo River Basin&gt;" target="&lt;Iron Tools for Farming&gt;">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">(The Congo) was a key region influenced by iron metallurgy as evidenced by farming practices. This suggests (tools), which improved productivity, were introduced or adopted here.)</data>
      <data key="d8">agricultural innovation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-41f85aebcdbec291afd82019b0842d65</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211071</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Introduction of Bronze Technology&gt;" target="&lt;Iron Tools for Farming&gt;">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">(The introduction) increased interest and understanding leading to (farming tools) from iron which directly superseded bronze methods. Bronze paved the way for iron by demonstrating that harder materials improved productivity.)</data>
      <data key="d8">technological advancement</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-41f85aebcdbec291afd82019b0842d65</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211071</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Central Africa (1000 BCE)&gt;" target="&lt;Iron Use by the Nok&gt;">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">(In Central Africa), early ironworking led to the Nok culture using metal tools, marking a significant technological leap that spread subsequently into Nok agricultural practices.)</data>
      <data key="d8">technological diffusion</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-41f85aebcdbec291afd82019b0842d65</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211071</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Iron Tools for Farming&gt;" target="&lt;Iron Use by the Nok&gt;">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">(Nok's use) of iron for tools and weapons was a precursor to broader (farming tool) adoption. This indicates the practical spread of ironworking beyond ceremonial uses.)</data>
      <data key="d8">metallic applications</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-41f85aebcdbec291afd82019b0842d65</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
