    <edge source="historical_figure" target="geographical_location">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Histories frequently revolve around the experiences and actions of notable individuals within specific geographic areas. These locations significantly impact, and in turn are impacted by, historical figures such as those discussed in "Not Just the Tudors." Discussions often center on the regions where these figures lived and worked, highlighting how their activities, influences, and lives were intrinsically linked to their geographical settings.</data>
      <data key="d8">Historic Influence,History,Location</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211107</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="historical_figure" target="source_or_artifact">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Historical figures are often showcased in various types of content, including podcasts such as "The History of Rome" and "Not Just the Tudors," which focus on individuals and events within detailed historical narratives. These media forms not only delve into the personal lives and actions of historical figures but also provide a broader context through their geographical settings, making them crucial for gaining a comprehensive understanding of both specific individuals and the broader periods in which they lived. Podcasts and similar audio content offer in-depth discussions about these historical figures within their respective contexts, enhancing listeners' comprehension of history beyond just isolated events or personalities.</data>
      <data key="d8">Contextual Narratives,Historical Content,Historical Figures,Individuals,Media</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6abf232f5832a47a95eb4ebe737fcbdd</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211109</data>
    </edge>
