      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">King Ezna of the Aksumite Kingdom played a significant role in both spiritual and territorial expansions during his rule. Notably, King Ezna converted the Aksumite Kingdom to Christianity through missionary efforts similar to those of Frumentius. This conversion marked an important cultural shift for the kingdom. Additionally, King Ezna was responsible for expanding and solidifying the Aksumite Kingdom's greatest extent during his reign, showcasing his political acumen and effectiveness as a ruler. His multifaceted contributions significantly enhanced both the religious and territorial landscape of the Aksumite Kingdom.</data>
