    <edge source="&lt;Delhi_Sultanate&gt;" target="&lt;Shajar_al-Durr&gt;">
      <data key="d6">7.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Shajar al-Durr was the widow of Iltutmish and played a significant role in the events surrounding the Delhi Sultanate during the succession struggle. She loyally supported Raziya but became instrumental in her downfall, marking a pivotal moment that led to her eventual rule. Shajar al-Durr's ascension to power highlighted the political instability and challenges associated with female rulership within the Delhi Sultanate, foreshadowing the complexities and turbulence of governance during this period.</data>
