    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Hundred Years' War&gt;" target="&lt;Great Western Schism">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;The Great Western Schism created divisions that could potentially exacerbate existing tensions between France and England, as both nations had interests in the Papal state's stability during this time. This relationship is moderate due to indirect connections through papacy influence on politics.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;political_division&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211097</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Hundred Years' War&gt;" target="&lt;The LandofCockaigne">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;Satirical works like The Land of Cockaigne could indirectly reflect contemporary societal conflicts, including those between England and France in the Hundred Years' War. While not direct, this relationship highlights the broader socio-political critiques present during the period.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;critique_of_medieval_conflicts&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211097</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;The LandofCockaigne&gt;" target="&lt;Pope Gregory XI">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;As a papal figure during the Great Western Schism, Pope Gregory XI's efforts to unify and reform the church could be seen as part of broader historical criticism, which The Land of Cockaigne parodies. This relationship is thematic rather than direct but reflects the larger social and religious context.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;church_unification_and_social_critique&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211097</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Pope Gregory XI&gt;" target="&lt;Hundred Years' War">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;The Hundred Years' War and the Great Western Schism both occurred during a period where religious and political upheaval were intertwined. The Papacy's weakened state due to schism could impact decisions and strategies taken by kings, including Edward III of England and Charles IV of France.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;schism_infuence_on_conflict&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211097</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Pope Gregory XI&gt;" target="&lt;Great Western Schism">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;The Great Western Schism directly involved Pope Gregory XI in efforts to unify the Papal court and address factional issues within the church. His return of the papacy to Rome was part of broader attempts at reconciliation.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;papal_unification&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211097</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;Pope Gregory XI&gt;" target="&lt;Holy Roman Empire">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;During the reign of Pope Gregory XI, there was an overlap in political and religious leadership between the Papacy and the Holy Roman Empire. The Emperor's role could indirectly influence church matters, though the direct interaction here is limited due to the specific nature of their positions.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;papal_empire_overlap&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211098</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;King Charles IV of France&gt;" target="&lt;Hundred Years' War">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;As a key figure in the early stages of the Hundred Years' War, King Charles IV's reign was marked by significant political and military events that directly involved his role as Holy Roman Emperor. His actions during this period significantly shaped French-German relations and European politics in general.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;charles_IV_leadership&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211097</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&lt;King Edward III of England&gt;" target="&lt;Hundred Years' War">
      <data key="d6">2.0</data>
      <data key="d7">&lt;The Hundred Years' War was a direct result of King Edward III's claims to the French throne, which were challenged by King Charles IV. This relationship is central as it outlines the primary cause and course of conflict between two key European powers during this period.</data>
      <data key="d8">&lt;conflict_cause_and_shape&gt;</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-6970ff4a745f78f3ab3bcab2da4945d1</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211098</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Little Ice Age" target="Great Famine">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The Great Famine and the climatic conditions during the Little Ice Age are correlated, with both occurring within a timeframe associated with cooling climate. The worsening environmental conditions contributed to the food shortages experienced.</data>
      <data key="d8">climate-famine</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f485cc659c371a55149fcc8ff3f200a5</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211098</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Little Ice Age" target="fourteenth century travel">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The difficulties of travel during the fourteenth century were exacerbated by the harsher climate conditions associated with the Little Ice Age, making it a significant challenge.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental-conditions</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f485cc659c371a55149fcc8ff3f200a5</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211099</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Little Ice Age" target="Black Death">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Both events occurred during the period of the Little Ice Age and interacted with its environmental impacts. The poor living conditions and weaker immune systems likely exacerbated the spread and impact of the Black Death.</data>
      <data key="d8">environmental-impact</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f485cc659c371a55149fcc8ff3f200a5</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211099</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Little Ice Age" target="plagues spread">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">During the Little Ice Age, environmental conditions may have supported denser rodent populations that could more easily carry and spread the plague.</data>
      <data key="d8">rodent-pestilence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f485cc659c371a55149fcc8ff3f200a5</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211099</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Little Ice Age" target="tree ring data">
      <data key="d6">6.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Tree ring data is used in studies of the Little Ice Age to reconstruct historical climates and understand the extent of cooling.</data>
      <data key="d8">climate-reconstruction</data>
