    </edge>
    <edge source="Marsilio Ficino" target="humanism">
      <data key="d6">12.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Marsilio Ficino's philosophical contributions to humanism helped shape the artistic practices of the period, including the emphasis on realism in paintings.</data>
      <data key="d8">philosophical influence</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-39f50645a1a52a72b5d8d61856942487</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211101</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Byzantine scholars" target="humanism">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The interaction with Byzantine scholars helped transmit knowledge that shaped the artistic approach in works like The Arnolfini Portrait.</data>
      <data key="d8">knowledge_transmission</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-39f50645a1a52a72b5d8d61856942487</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211101</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Scientific Revolution" target="Nicholas Cusanus">
      <data key="d6">20.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Nicholas Cusanus had a significant impact on the development during the Scientific Revolution.</data>
      <data key="d8">Influence</data>
