    <edge source="&quot;Rebellions'" target="Chief Minister Position ">
      <data key="d6">4.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The abolition of the chief minister position contributed to reducing the likelihood of internal rebellions by dismantling potential rivals or checks on the emperor's power, highlighting a relationship between administrative reforms and stability.</data>
