    <edge source="Nomadic Societies Decline" target="Technological Changes">
      <data key="d6">8.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Technological advancements, particularly firearm technology, played a significant role in the decline of nomadic societies by making it harder for them to defend against settled communities with larger resources and superior weaponry." "&lt;br&gt;The key aspect here is how new technologies influenced societal changes over time." </data>
      <data key="d8">historical event,military impact,technological change</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f3acbd758cf8087488127fa375dda8fa</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211105</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nomadic Societies Decline" target="Life of Nomadic Societies">
      <data key="d6">17.0</data>
      <data key="d7">The decline of Nomadic Societies is a complex process that significantly impacts and is shaped by the experiences of its individual members. This relationship underscores how broader socio-historical changes affect daily life at an intimate level, influencing both the personal circumstances and the integration or marginalization of nomadic individuals into new systems. The decline of these societies fundamentally alters the lives of their members, reflecting a reciprocal interaction where societal transformations are directly influenced by the lived experiences and responses of those affected.</data>
      <data key="d8">historical event,history,individual impact,life conditions,social change,societal change</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-f3acbd758cf8087488127fa375dda8fa</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211107</data>
    </edge>
