    <edge source="Nomadic Culture" target="Pastoralism">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Nomadic cultures on the Inner Asian Steppe were centered around pastoralism, adopting lifestyles adapted to frequent relocation for grazing pastures, reflecting a deep cultural attachment to herding practices.</data>
      <data key="d8">Lifestyle Adaptation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e0736691e54b25ececc6a59ab1799e43</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
      <data key="d11">1783211056</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="Nomadic Culture" target="Horseback Riding">
      <data key="d6">10.0</data>
      <data key="d7">Horseback riding was a key adaptation driven by the needs of nomadic cultures on the Inner Asian Steppe, enabling them to manage large herds and navigate challenging terrains effectively.</data>
      <data key="d8">Skill Adaptation</data>
      <data key="d9">chunk-e0736691e54b25ececc6a59ab1799e43</data>
      <data key="d10">dumps/World_History_Volume_1/pages_content.json</data>
